.TH expr_eval 3 2026-10-23 "Graph Drawer expr man-pages 1.0.13"
.SH NAME
expr_eval \- expression evaluator
.SH LIBRARY
Graph Drawer Expression Evaluator Library
.RI ( libexpr ,\~ \-lexpr )
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.BR #include\~"expr.h"
.P
.BI "double expr_eval(const struct expr *" ep ",double " input ");"
.BI "int expr_step(const struct expr *restrict " ep " ,expr_t " input ",expr_t *restrict " output ",struct expr_inst **restrict " saveip ");"
.BI "expr_t expr_callback(const struct expr *restrict " ep ",expr_t " input ",const struct expr_callback *" ec ");"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.BR expr_eval()
function evaluates the
.B struct expr
object
.I ep
with the argument
.IR input ,
corresponding to the
.I asym
argument in
.BR expr_new()
and
.BR expr_init() .
.P
The
.BR expr_step()
function evaluates the
.B struct expr
object
.I ep
step-by-step, the
.I *saveip
must be set to
.I ep->data
at the start.
.P
The
.BR expr_callback()
function evaluates the
.B struct expr
object
.I ep
and run the callback function at the begin and end of each instruments.
.SH RETURN VALUE
The
.BR expr_eval() , expr_callback()
returns the result of the evaluation.
.P
The
.BR expr_step()
returns 1 if completed and write the result to
.I *output
or 0 if not completed.
.SH ATTRIBUTES
.TS
allbox;
lbx lb lb
l l l.
Interface	Attribute	Value
T{
.na
.nh
.BR expr_eval() , expr_step() , expr_callback()
T}	Thread safety	MT-Safe
.TE
